\given A bipartite cubic graph $G = (L \cup P, E)$.
\question Is $G$ the incidence (Levi) graph of a geometric $3$-configuration, that is, are there points for $P$, and lines for $L$ such that $E$ has an edge $p\ell$ if and only if $p$ is incident to $\ell$?
\complexity In \ER.
