I can read it as `to compute a \ensuremath{(\mathrm 1\;\Varid{+}\;\Var k)}-sublist of \ensuremath{\Var x\;\Varid{∷}\;\Var xs} and pass it to continuation~\ensuremath{\Var p}, either compute a \ensuremath{(\mathrm 1\;\Varid{+}\;\Var k)}-sublist \ensuremath{\Var ys} of \ensuremath{\Var xs} and pass \ensuremath{\Var ys} to \ensuremath{\Var p} directly, or compute a \ensuremath{\Var k}-sublist \ensuremath{\Var zs} of \ensuremath{\Var xs} and pass \ensuremath{\Var x\;\Varid{∷}\;\Var zs} to~\ensuremath{\Var p}'.
