The cases for \ensuremath{\Con{tip_s}\;\anonymous } and \ensuremath{\Con{bin}\;\anonymous \;(\Con{tip_s}\;\anonymous )} can be eliminated immediately since the side condition \ensuremath{\Var k\;\unskip<\ignorenext\;\Var n} is violated.
I go straight to the last and the most difficult case, \ensuremath{\Con{bin}\;\Var t\;\Var u}, where \ensuremath{\Var t}~and~\ensuremath{\Var u} are both constructed by \ensuremath{\Con{bin}}.
Their types are
