\subsection{\uppercase{Direct Extraction}}
\label{sec:direct-extraction}
The direct extraction process involves extracting the desired information object directly from a given input string, which may be either a compressed HTML page or its plain text content. To parse the extracted information into a predefined Pydantic data model, we make use of the \texttt{response\_format} parameter provided in the official OpenAI\footnote{OpenAI Package: \url{https://github.com/openai/openai-python}, last visited 30.03.2025.} Python package.

The corresponding flow chart in Figure~\ref{fig:flowcharts} illustrates the simplicity of this approach. Each product page is processed separately: After preprocessing, the page is passed to the \texttt{o3-mini} model along with a prompt that specifies the required information objects and the expected output format.


