Let $C_k$ denote the portion of the common stream rate that is allocated to user-$k$. Inherently, $C_k \geq 0$, $\forall k$, and $\sum_k C_k = R_\text{c}$. The rate experienced by user-$k$ is given by\footnote{Hereinafter, the superscript "SIC/non-SIC" indicates that the expression depends on whether SIC receivers or non-SIC receivers are used.}
\begin{equation}
    R_k^{\text{SIC/non-SIC}} = C_k + R_{\text{p},k}^{\text{SIC/non-SIC}}.
\end{equation}
