We first evaluate the sum-rate performance by setting $[u_1,...,u_k] = \mathbf{1}^{1\times K}$. Figure \ref{SR} depicts the ergodic sum-rate of SIC-based and SIC-free RSMA under finite constellations. The performance of SDMA under finite constellations is also depicted by fixing the transmission mode to be the first one in each dictionaries. Furthermore, the performance of RSMA and SDMA under Gaussian distributed input signals, generated following \cite{Mao_EURASIP}, is included as a reference. It can be observed that, in all cases, SIC-free RSMA preserves most of the superiority of SIC-based RSMA over SDMA, which is consistent with the conclusion in \cite{Sibo2024}.

