%------------------------------------------%
\section{Conclusion}
In conclusion, in this work, we aimed to investigate the fundamental limits of SIC-based and SIC-free RSMA under finite constellations. We first derived the rate expressions for SIC-based and SIC-free RSMA. We then proposed precoding optimization algorithms for WSR and MMF optimization problems. To enable these optimization algorithms in large-scale systems with feasible computational burden,  we introduced user grouping, null space projection and dimensionality reduction techniques. Numerical results show that RSMA schemes outperform SDMA under finite constellations with either WSR or MMF optimization, similar to the Gaussian distributed inputs. Furthermore, SIC-free RSMA preserves most of the superiority of SIC-based RSMA, which extends the conclusion in \cite{Sibo2024} from low-complexity precoders to fully optimized precoders, from sum-rate objective to WSR and MMF objectives, and from small-scale systems to large-scale systems.
